GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\opus_p1.md:98:+	/*  #503: bound reassert_interrupts() to the slots connected below;
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\opus_p1.md:129:- **grok's M_STOREBUTNOREASSERT escapes — and I measured why.** M_NOREASSERT (SOFT arm's `reassert_interrupts(d)` deleted) scores 20/20 + 8/8. Deleting the *device-line* handlers' reassert calls as well (M_NOREASSERT2) reds `slot0 deliver`. **So the clock's own reassert carries the delivery**: `reassert_interrupts()` has four call sites, and any device line re-runs the whole loop. A free-running row proves *the loop delivers*, never *this call site ran*. That call site is outside the (a) diff, so it is disclosed coverage debt, not a floor cell — and it independently confirms the brief's corollary that on a running guest the next device interrupt re-enters the loop.
