GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\fixreview_20260904\fable5_adjudication.md:8:**VERDICT: GO-WITH-CHANGES.** The FIX is correct block-by-block and refuses NOTHING the one in-tree guest (OpenBSD 2.2/mvme187) does. No previous repair is live-wrong (the one that was -- pass-10's ICLR store-mask claim -- is already reverted). Part 12 finds ZERO floor breaches: all three TxCTL enumeration mutants die. Two cheap, non-design changes gate a valid close: (a) gate-14 has NOT been run on the live probe (`<<GATE14_P12_OWED>>` unfilled; the live probe got a post-table docstring edit, so its 242/242 is inferred, not measured); (b) `pcc2c040kill` is NOT rightly the only HIGH -- `pcc2defaultkill` is an equal host-kill class with more plausible real-boot reachability and is filed severity-untagged.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\fixreview_20260904\fable5_adjudication.md:14:- **Reads ACCEPT by fall-through is right.** The top-of-function `memcpy` serves raw bytes in address order (width-correct). Every store sits under `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)`, so a fall-through read never stores. SCCRXIACK (0x27) is the 13th arm -- no width guard, ignores `idata`, INT-clear side effect width-invariant -- correctly excluded from the twelve. IPL's read-side print is width-invariant too. No block's read has a side effect the memcpy skips.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\fixreview_20260904\fable5_adjudication.md:28:## Q3 -- ORDERED DISPOSITION. `pcc2c040kill` is NOT the only HIGH.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\fixreview_20260904\fable5_adjudication.md:31:2. **`pcc2c040kill` -- HIGH, fix next (rank below defaultkill).** Legal `st.b 0x04` to GENCTL -> reassert -> C040 -> `exit(1)`. Lower trigger bar than a width kill, but the in-tree guest has **no genctl write at all** and C040 is 68040-companion mode an 88100 never enables -- so NOT boot-reachable by the shipped guest; witness synthetic (`put b 0xfff42002, 0x04`). Different predicate from defaultkill (value-in-callee vs decode) -> separate round.
