GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:25:**Setup, verified from source (not ratified):** guard is `if (len != 1 && writeflag == MEM_WRITE)` (`dev_pcc2.c:511`). The guarded body (`:513-543`) reads both pending counts and **tests `> 0` on each** (`:528`, `:533`; `reassert_interrupts` `:277`, `:280`). So `(pending1, pending2)` is a product of two body-tested `{0,>0}` partitions — that is the fact that puts the joint cell on the table.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:86:`dev_pcc2.c`: full `DEVICE_ACCESS` switch (12 arms), helper, `pcc_timer_tick`, `reassert_interrupts`, `DEVICE_TICK`, width-bit enum, struct, `mvme_pcctworeg.h` defines; diffed in full vs `b78bb0f`. Probe: `session()`, `enc`, `program/program_free`, `setup`, `armval/cval`, all arm builders + sessions, `row()`, `BLOCKS12`. Measured: `BASE/M_PENDBOTH/M_TXCTL_OVFHI.out`, `driver.log`, `PRETABLE_pass9.out` (disk + mtime), `gate14_p10.log`. `gate_arm.sh` diff, CLAUDE.md amendment. Floor cells checked for a surviving breach: pending 2×2 (closed), single-operand `idata` (`idata!=2` escapes → disclosed), `TxICR 0x37`/`TxCTL 0xff` (disclosed). **No fresh mutant table** (read-only seat); the named escapes are derived from the row set + source and are consistent with the measured `M_PENDBOTH`/`M_TXCTL_OVFHI` behaviour. Premises **not** independently settled (named, not ratified): the OpenBSD clock/statclock steady-state claim (corroboration only — reachability is measured directly by the row); an exhaustive tree-wide grep for external pokes of `pending_*` (in-file writers confirmed; the device owns the field).
